# Title: Suspicious New Service Creation
# ID: 17a1be64-8d88-40bf-b5ff-a4f7a50ebcc8
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-07-14
# Tags: attack.persistence, attack.privilege-escalation, attack.t1543.003
# Description: Detects creation of a new service via "sc" command or the powershell "new-service" cmdlet with suspicious binary paths
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((cmdline:*New-Service* AND cmdline:*-BinaryPathName*)) OR (process_name:*\\sc.exe AND (cmdline:*create* AND cmdline:*binPath=*))) AND ((cmdline:*powershell* OR cmdline:*mshta* OR cmdline:*wscript* OR cmdline:*cscript* OR cmdline:*svchost* OR cmdline:*dllhost* OR cmdline:*cmd * OR cmdline:*cmd.exe /c* OR cmdline:*cmd.exe /k* OR cmdline:*cmd.exe /r* OR cmdline:*rundll32* OR cmdline:*C:\\Users\\Public* OR cmdline:*\\Downloads\\* OR cmdline:*\\Desktop\\* OR cmdline:*\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\Startup\\* OR cmdline:*C:\\Windows\\TEMP\\* OR cmdline:*\\AppData\\Local\\Temp*)))
